From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:39:19 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 70/76] flashnext cuda: TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARD_HEAD's greedy verify
 exchanges each half's best rows, not the scores

With TF_FLASHNEXT_SHARD_HEAD=1 at --tp 2 each rank projects its half of the
vocabulary, then gathered every row's 124,160 bf16 scores one row at a time
before rank 0's fn_row_best. A verify pass whose windows are all greedy and
unmasked (and TF_FLASHNEXT_VERIFY_HOST_LOGITS off) now runs fn_row_best_part
on its half instead: fn_row_best's scan and folds (first id on ties), plus a
flag for any NaN or +Inf, the id offset by the rank's base. One gatherF32 of
rows x 16 bytes brings both ranks' rows; rank 0 merges them on the host
(proposal_rows.mergeParts: larger best, a tie the lower column, the lse slot
NaN where the whole row's would be non-finite), so pickBest returns the same
token or the same ProposalNonfinite. Rank 0 decides per verify frame and sends
the choice as flag 1 on verify and verify_many; such a pass runs eagerly.
Sampled, masked or host-logit passes keep the per-row score gather.

The switch now splits only --tp 2 ranks; one GPU and --pp 2 stages keep the
whole head instead of refusing to load. The contract test merges
fn_row_best_part's two halves against fn_row_best's pick and refusals.
